{"kind":"promise","text":"Promised. Both blockers, the same-head architecture correction, mutation proofs, the seven-plus-diff artifact set, then review from codex. I will not merge.\n\nHOW I INTEND TO FIX THE FIRST ONE, stated now so you can stop me if it is the wrong shape. The defect is that --local bounds which configuration file is read and not which repository Git resolves, so GIT_DIR, GIT_WORK_TREE, GIT_COMMON_DIR and their relatives redirect the read to another repository entirely. I reproduced it before asking you for this row and I will re-derive it as a failing regression first, so the test is written against the behaviour I want rather than the behaviour I have. Your conditions say to reuse the existing environment-sanitization model rather than add a second repository resolver, and I agree — a second resolver would be a third opinion about which repository we are in, which is how this class of defect gets reintroduced. So I will find where the codebase already sanitizes the Git environment and route this read through it.\n\nWHAT I WILL PROVE, not assert. That LocalRepo and /v0/worktrees cannot expose a remote injected through any of those variables — both surfaces, not just the one nearest the fix, because the whole point of the finding is that the guard I thought I had was in the wrong place. And by mutation that each new regression fails when its guard is broken; a green test proves nothing about coverage.\n\nTHE SECOND ONE. Reject the raw \"?\" and \"#\" delimiters before net/url.Parse ever sees the string, with a bare-# regression beside the existing bare-? case. Parsing first is what created the divergence: Go's parser silently drops a bare trailing \"#\" and re-serializes without it, while the browser's URL preserves it and refuses. Checking the raw bytes is both the fix and the simplification codex asked for.\n\nTHE ARCHITECTURE PAGE. Its \"repository-local configuration only\" line is a contract I published and the code did not have. It moves in the same head as the code, not after it.\n\nWHAT WOULD MAKE ME COME BACK TO YOU. If the environment-sanitization model turns out not to exist in a reusable form, or if binding the read to the resolved repository needs a change outside the seven paths, I will stop and assert on this promise rather than widen it myself. I have an open widening request on the MCP lane right now for exactly that reason, and I would rather ask twice than assume once."}